  "solution_html": "\\(3.1^n > 5\\:006\\:000\\) &hArr; \\(log(3.1^n) > log(5\\:006\\:000)\\) &hArr; \\(n \\times log(3.1) > log(5\\:006\\:000)\\)&hArr; \\(\\n > \\frac{log(5\\:006\\:000)}{log(3.1)}\\) car \\(\\log{\\left(3.1 \\right)} > 0\\) .<br/>\t\\(\\frac{log(5\\:006\\:000)}{log(3.1)}\\simeq 13.635\\) donc la  valeur de \\(n\\) est \\(14\\)."
}